{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce mandatory licensing for all barbers and barber shop owners",
        "additional_details": "Barbers use sharp tools and work closely with clients, making hygiene, safety and skill essential. Yet there is no mandatory national qualification or licence to work as or own a barber shop in the UK. We believe the Government should introduce a licensing system with recognised training or competency standards to improve public safety, raise industry standards, and also to prevent any unqualified barbers from owning a shop \u2013 meaning barbershops will be run and owned by barbers for the good of the barbers\u2019 profession.",
        "background": "We want the Government to introduce a licensing system requiring anyone working as or owning a barber shop to hold a recognised barbering qualification or meet an approved national standard. We believe this protects both customers and qualified barbers.",
